    "result_text": "Only one test class exists in the project (the acceptance test), and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema, documenting the format (`'+61412345678'` \u2192 `'+61 412 345 678'`) and that raw `telephone` stays E.164. This is what generates the field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 A standalone formatter helper (matching the existing `OwnerLocality`/`CustomerCodeCheckDigit` pattern, kept off the mapper so MapStruct doesn't treat it as an implicit String conversion). It splits off the longest known E.164 country code (`61`, `1`), then renders `+<cc>` + space + national digits grouped in threes from the left. Null/blank/no-digit inputs pass through unchanged.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Imported `TelephoneDisplay` and added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` computed from `owner.getTelephone()` at read time, alongside the other derived fields.\n\nThe acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (input `\"0412 345 678\"` \u2192 `telephone` = `\"+61412345678\"`, `telephoneDisplay` = `\"+61 412 345 678\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
